<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">On the opening night of Web Summit in Lisb=
on, the Nvidia CEO, Jensen Huang=E2=80=99s admission that he had an affair =
with a Chinese datacenter executive suspected to be a spy for Beijing hit t=
he main stage. The news broke less than 24 hours prior, and the reaction wa=
s surprising.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Matthew Prince, CEO of Cloudflare, broaden=
ed the implications of the scandal from Huang=E2=80=99s personal life to Nv=
idia=E2=80=99s market dominance.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CWhatever Jensen did in his person=
al life, that=E2=80=99s very salacious. In the longer term, whether Nvidia =
is the hero or the villain, we=E2=80=99ll be asking: Were the things they d=
id to cement their market position =E2=80=A6 just financial engineering?=E2=
=80=9D Prince said in front of tens of thousands of onlookers.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Nvidia=E2=80=99s essential role in the AI =
boom as the world=E2=80=99s premier chipmaker had given it a Teflon reputat=
ion in Silicon Valley. It served as both a bank =E2=80=93 providing loans t=
o its own buyers to purchase its chips =E2=80=93 and hardware provider. Pri=
nce credited Huang for doing =E2=80=9Ca lot to cement the AI ecosystem=E2=
=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Likewise asked to respond to the news, Ric=
hard Socher, CEO of the four-month-old AI startup Recursive Superintelligen=
ce, simply said he was =E2=80=9Cgrateful to have Jensen in my corner=E2=80=
=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Prince responded immediately: =E2=80=9CTha=
t=E2=80=99s captured interest!=E2=80=9D After all, Nvidia participated in R=
ecursive=E2=80=99s $500m investment round, announced in April. The chipmake=
r has <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLM=
EmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEA13-uHzzNLsl3ZqJFCJlFeBPAqLFFGr911WDq0uP=
YgjWwSku3ZEDz9wo3APw7QVnmtklNEP8_PrtnQmJZFOMhauhi8ooOFEBKC828qX4PcJYp3p9TFo=
d52_hPW7gDK2Q7u-YOusa618XpbqaC5bsMq5SOSuELdRPatymSxy7yEDVtNSYLNsxyoEwm7yQPx=
5UNEhaesZqKIAJSmOxHBcClNqTAUVWZHTclL7I1p7PWtgNp933xve3QBFqhyZHJyj2sGX9vdvI_=
px1sX7-bmpFyMdNJR2mVUdHoQMQfpfEEX0Q/4vm/oyfknYPzQlaG_x14c5lUcg/h19/h001.vGc=
hJ8eUkY0NoU7ql5SapDEEJJTL5ahA2nfLSbSj9UE" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">faced c=
riticism</a> over its circular financing deals, but the superiority of its =
hardware has for many years allowed it to make strong alliances within Sili=
con Valley that have warded off lasting damage.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">US intelligence agencies are already scrut=
inizing Huang. Judging by Prince=E2=80=99s remarks, Silicon Valley may soon=
 do the same.</p>
