<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In the wake of Tuesday=E2=80=99s blue wave=
, Silicon Valley is attempting to reconcile with the new power brokers in t=
he US.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Tech=E2=80=99s tycoons spent the last two =
years cozying up to Donald Trump. On Thursday, Elon Musk sang a different t=
une. After railing against Texas Democrat James Talarico with jibes like =
=E2=80=9CHe=E2=80=99ll trans your kids=E2=80=9D and spending tens of millio=
ns to elect his opponent, Musk responded kindly when the senator-elect call=
ed him a =E2=80=9Cgreat innovator=E2=80=9D on a podcast. Musk tweeted: =E2=
=80=9CNice of him to say that=E2=80=9D. How cordial! It=E2=80=99s a far cry=
 from the extreme and unrelenting partisanship that Musk has hawked for mon=
ths leading up to the elections.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Venture capitalist Chamath Palihapitiya, h=
ost of the influential All-In podcast, <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.=
theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.QvkQtXiSzSINXrMyEJiuYj4DeghJb-Z4JzGlxFd_HGz4FNyPR=
qiXr3ZPTfVPzmsIBTSnUDl0gGdSNeuemzaIciify_TS5k01uqQc8TwTUnBfhyhl9d_9R9KSN5ZT=
Bv9id2IUhZi3CPYz53nIn-lRdJprpPO_Nr-Wb8eQELtvh15VWjRCOYq824cdlXyw26L6offX9bU=
bqnE1xKmdRZlm7gw8ecYL9r3BeU8gJQBR6PY/4vm/oyfknYPzQlaG_x14c5lUcg/h20/h001.xm=
kZswtaWDsE-5xN_yNlM0HKyIMFRY4H0qPVV1RRn9s" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">tweete=
d</a> on Sunday: =E2=80=9CWhen I=E2=80=99m wrong, I=E2=80=99m wrong =E2=80=
=A6 This was a complete and total repudiation about the state of the econom=
y. The economy is broken.=E2=80=9D His message sounds much closer to afford=
ability-obsessed Democrats.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Democratic lawmakers are putting out state=
ments that any reconciliation by the tech oligarchy remains largely one-sid=
ed and transactional. Newly in-control Democrats do seem to differ in their=
 views on the best strategy for dealing with the conservative problem of Si=
licon Valley. Members of Congress are eager to haul in tech CEOs for grilli=
ngs and pass AI safety laws. Newly elected governors campaigned on promises=
 of moratoria on datacenter construction.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It is not clear which is the best path for=
ward for Democrats as they assume power. The US stock market relies heavily=
 on the AI industry=E2=80=99s growth. Hamstringing that industry with bans =
on new datacenters and legislation that cracks down on AI model development=
 risks sending the economy into a backslide. However, the voting public wan=
ts to make a public example of AI CEOs, who are despised on both sides of t=
he aisle despite their alliance with Trump and the Republican elite.</p>
